  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"&#8970;\" close=\"&#8971;\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. The number of matrices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> such that the sum of all entries is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> prime number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is _____ ."
  },
